---
title: Kokumaro Curry (House Foods)
description: A rich yet mild Japanese curry made with a blend of two different kinds of roux.
servings: 8
time required: 45m
source: https://housefoods-group.com/products/en/recipe/kokumaro.html
author: House Foods
tags: [curry, japanese, stew, rice]
cuisine: japanese
---

> The recipe is the same for mild, medium hot, and hot Kokumaro Curry Sauce Mix.
> For 4 servings, halve everything and use 2 1/2 cups (600 ml) of water, or
> 2 cups (500 ml) if cooking in a covered pot. Serve over rice.

Preheat @vegetable oil{2%tbsp} in a #pot{} over medium heat. Add @chicken breast{300%g}
(cut into bite-size pieces), @onions{2}(cut into bite-size pieces),
@potatoes{2}(cut into bite-size pieces), and @carrot{1}(cut into bite-size
pieces), and sauté well until the onions are lightly browned.

Add @water{4 1/5%cups} and simmer over low to medium heat until the ingredients
soften, about ~{15%minutes}. If cooking in a covered pot, use 3 1/2 cups
(850 ml) instead.

Remove from the heat. Break apart @Kokumaro Curry Sauce Mix{1%box} into the pot
and stir until dissolved.

Return to low heat and simmer once more, stirring occasionally, until the curry
thickens, about ~{10%minutes}.

> Optional: to add honey, add it in step 2, and after bringing the curry to a
> boil, simmer for at least ~{20%minutes}.
